  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Place simmer sauce, veggies, mango, salt, and pepper in a large skillet, then stir to combine the curry. Bring curry to a boil over high heat, stirring occasionally. Once boiling, reduce heat and simmer until veggies and mango are just tender, 4-5 minutes.",
      "secondary_message": "1 (425 g) jar Indian mango curry sauce\n2 cups frozen mixed vegetables\n1 cup frozen mango\n⅛ tsp salt\n⅛ tsp black pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, if using frozen shrimp, place them in a colander and run under cold water to thaw them slightly and remove any ice crystals. (If using fresh shrimp, skip this step.) Place the shrimp on a clean towel or paper towels and pat dry. ",
      "secondary_message": "340 g raw shrimp, peeled & deveined, fresh or frozen"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Add shrimp to the curry and stir to combine; return to a simmer and continue to cook until shrimp are cooked through, 4-5 minutes more. Remove from heat.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, squeeze pouches to separate rice, then tear a two-inch opening at the top of each to vent. Place both packages in the microwave and heat on high until warmed through, 2-2 1/2 minutes. Carefully remove from microwave and set aside to cool slightly.",
      "secondary_message": "2 (240 g) pouch basmati rice, pre-cooked"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "To serve, divide rice and curry between bowls. Enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
